  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n   - We use a multi-start evolutionary strategy combined with Gaussian Process (GP) regression to guide the search towards promising regions while enforcing the integral constraint.\n   - This differs from the local search of the original SA by combining global exploration (GP-based Bayesian optimization) with constrained optimization.\n   - The main bottleneck is escaping local optima, which is addressed by maintaining an archive of elite candidates and using GP to propose diverse moves. We project onto allowed regions using pyramid segments to reduce drift.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   - Representation: Symmetric step function defined by its first half-vector `h` of length `n_half = n_points//2`.\n   - Integral constraint: `\u222bh(x)dx = 1` requires `\u2211h[i] = n_points/4` (verified via discrete integration).\n   - Objective: Minimize `C_5 = max_k (\u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx)` computed via:\n        `C_5_max = dx * max(np.correlate(np.concatenate([h, h[::-1]]), 1-np.concatenate([h, h[::-1]]), mode='full'))`\n   - Repair operations:\n        - Integral repair: Preserve sum via post-processing scaling.\n        - Boundary projection: Ensure values stay in bounds `[0,1]` using six-sided pressure matrices.\n   - Dimensionality control: Focus search in 4-pyramid regions defined by length scales `L, M, S`.\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   - Initialization:\n     - n_points = input dimension (default 280)\n     - dx = 2.0 / n_points\n     - integral_target = n_points/4\n     - If `initial_h_values` available: start with parent, else use uniform initialization.\n   - GP regression:\n     - Use Mat\u00e9rn kernel with \u03bd=2.5\n     - Model y=f(x) where x-vector \u2208 [0,1]^{n_half}\n     - Objective function `neg_overlap(x)` returns `-C_5` with internal repair.\n   - Evolution loop (main search):\n     - Maintain archive { (x, neg_val) } for top candidates\n     - Sample proposal from Gaussian process predictive + noise\n     - Apply multi-start local search from the most recent improved point\n     - Update GP with new samples\n     - Project all vectors through repair operator if integral deviates\n   - Repair algorithm:\n     - Input: vector and optional target sum\n     - Steps: (1) Clip values to [0,1] (2) Scale to exact sum\n   - Local tuner:\n     - Use L-BFGS-B with bounds to minimize residual sum around current best\n     - Constraints strictly enforced via repair\n   - Timers:\n     - Main search: 90% for GP+local search\n     - Final safety: 10% for fertility check ($ measure diversity)\n\n4. Search choices and variations:\n   - Base case:\n     - Local window factor f_local = 0.5\n     - Dim-reduction threshold thr_dim = 5.0\n     - Projection intensity = dependent on local energy surface\n   - Variants:\n     - Apocalypse at cost threshold 25: major dimension cutback > thr_dim\n     - Comet trail path: penalize excessive return-to-origin\n   - Hyperparameter sweep:\n     - (f_local_low = 0.2, f_local_high = 0.8)\n     - (thr_dim_low = 2.0, thr_dim_high = 7.0)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness:\n   - Primary cost: Correlation Jacobian inspection for GP\n   - Typical:\n     - Correlation: O(n_points^2) ~ 78,400 operations per eval\n     - GP updates: O(n_half^2 * num_sam) ~ 19,600 * 50 = 980k ops\n   - Safeguard: Exit if 90% of budget has passed with no improvement\n   - Recovery: Valid fallback uses parent if out of bounds\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n   - Feasibility checks:\n     - sum(h) \u2208 (integral_target-1e-6, integral_target+1e-6)\n     - C_5 computed independently\n   - Consistency enforcements:\n     - Final solution re-clipped and scaled\n     - Timer clearly notes completion progress\n   - Interface:\n     - Output metrics: (h_values, c5_bound, n_points)\n     - h_values normalized to second-half coordinates",
